  "evidencia": "Page: Little Missouri River (North Dakota). Sentence: The Little Missouri River is a tributary of the Missouri River, 560 miles (901 km) long, in the northern Great Plains of the United States.\nPage: Little Missouri River (North Dakota). Sentence: Rising in northeastern Wyoming, in western Crook County about 15 miles (24 km) west of Devils Tower, it flows northeastward, across a corner of southeastern Montana, and into South Dakota.\nPage: Devils Tower. Sentence: Devils Tower (also Bear Lodge Butte) is a laccolithic butte composed of igneous rock in the Bear Lodge Mountains (part of the Black Hills) near Hulett and Sundance in Crook County, northeastern Wyoming, above the Belle Fourche River.\nPage: Devils Tower. Sentence: It rises dramatically 1,267 feet (386 m) above the Belle Fourche River, standing 867 feet (265 m) from summit to base.\nPage: Three V Crossing, North Dakota. Sentence: Three V Crossing is located on the Little Missouri River 19.1 mi north-northeast of Marmarth.",
