        "original_id": "431617ae-c2cc-5418-8292-979550962dd0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Little Missouri River, Devils Tower, Three V Crossing, Missouri River, Belle Fourche River, Bear Lodge Mountains, Black Hills, Marmarth\n- Topics: River course, landforms, geographic measurements\n\nFacts:\n- The Little Missouri River is a 560-mile tributary of the Missouri River in the northern Great Plains of the United States.\n- The Little Missouri River rises in northeastern Wyoming in western Crook County about 15 miles west of Devils Tower.\n- The Little Missouri River flows northeast across a corner of southeastern Montana and into South Dakota.\n- Devils Tower, also called Bear Lodge Butte, is a laccolithic igneous butte in the Bear Lodge Mountains of the Black Hills near Hulett and Sundance in Crook County, northeastern Wyoming, above the Belle Fourche River.\n- Devils Tower rises 1,267 feet above the Belle Fourche River and stands 867 feet from summit to base.\n- Three V Crossing is on the Little Missouri River 19.1 miles north-northeast of Marmarth.",
